// A specialization that folds an operand to a panic leaves an operator whose
// operand diverges: `panic(…) * 0`, `-panic(…)`. The operator keeps the width
// its type says, i64 here, rather than one read off the never-typed operand.
use { println, Stdout } from "core:cli";

fn length_of(unit: i32) -> i64 {
    return match unit {
        0 => 1,
        1 => 1000,
        _ => panic(`unit ${unit} has no fixed length`),
    };
}

fn most_of(unit: i32) -> i64 {
    return match unit {
        0 => 1000,
        1 => 60,
        _ => 0,
    };
}

fn span_of(unit: i32) -> i64 {
    return length_of(unit) * most_of(unit);
}

fn back_of(unit: i32) -> i64 {
    return -length_of(unit);
}

fn wide_of(unit: i32) -> f64 {
    return length_of(unit) as f64;
}

export fn run() with Stdout {
    println(`${span_of(0)} ${span_of(1)} ${back_of(1)} ${wide_of(1)}`);
    if builtin::black_box(false) {
        println(`${span_of(2)} ${back_of(2)} ${wide_of(2)}`);
    }
}

__DATA__
{
    "stdout": "1000 60000 -1000 1000\n"
}
